ividually. You must be able to show that the criteria were applied fairly and that ethnicity played no part in the decision. - **Document legitimate individual performance issues only where they exist.** If particular employees, regardless of ethnicity, have documented, recent performance or conduct problems that are relevant to your criteria, those can be considered—but only if they are part of a uniformly applied system. The outcome of a fair process might well include some Hispanic employees and exclude others, but the selection itself cannot be based on their ethnicity. If you are uncertain how to proceed, please treat this as a serious compliance risk and get professional guidance before you take another step.
